Console Order Management System

-Description
This project is a simple program that runs in the console. It helps manage a small business by allowing you to register clients, products, and create orders. It also shows reports about sales and income.

This system works like a digital notebook where everything is organized automatically.

How to open and run the project (step by step)

Open Visual Studio Code (VS Code)

Go to your computer and open the program called “Visual Studio Code”.

Open the project folder

Click on "File" (top menu)

Select "Open Folder"

Look for the folder named "registro"

Select it and click "Open"

Open the terminal

In VS Code, go to the top menu

Click on "Terminal"

Then click on "New Terminal"

Run the program

In the terminal, type the following command:

python main.py

Press Enter

Use the system

A menu will appear on the screen

Type a number and press Enter to choose an option

Project Structure

The project is organized into several files, each one with a specific function:

main.py
This is the main file. It shows the menu and connects all parts of the system.

Clientes.py
Handles client registration.

Producto.py
Handles product registration.

Pedido.py
Manages order creation.

Visualizarpedido.py
Allows you to view a specific order.

totaldia.py
Calculates the total income of the day.

reporte.py
Generates the final report with all sales information.

What the system can do

Register clients

Register products

Create orders

View orders

Calculate total daily income

Generate a final report

How it works

When you run the program, you will see a menu like this:

Register client

Register product

Create order

View orders

View daily income

View final report

Exit

You just choose an option by typing a number.

The system will ask for the necessary information, such as names, IDs, prices, and quantities.

